 ## Background
-Binary Greedy Meshing was developed as an optimization for voxel graphics, leveraging bitwise operations to accelerate the greedy meshing process. It was popularized in the context of Lua-based voxel engines (e.g., Roblox) and C++ voxel engines (e.g., OloEngine) [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. The method treats the voxel volume as a binary field and uses bitwise tricks to find maximal rectangles, significantly outperforming traditional run-based greedy meshing in terms of clock cycles [S2, unofficial].
